# Every path through the sample, ready to send from Visual Studio, Rider or the VS Code REST client.
# The data is in memory: restart the sample to reset it.

@host = http://localhost:57742
@ada = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@bob = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@cleo = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@dan = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004
@eve = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005

### Cleo is signed up and in no tenant yet -> 204
POST {{host}}/users/{{cleo}}/assign

### Dan has not signed up -> 409 /problems/user/not-signed-up, thrown from the service
POST {{host}}/users/{{dan}}/assign

### Bob already belongs to acme -> 409 /problems/user/already-assigned
POST {{host}}/users/{{bob}}/assign

### Nobody has this id -> 404 /problems/user/unknown, declared once on the controller
POST {{host}}/users/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000099/assign

### One of Ada's orders -> 200
GET {{host}}/users/{{ada}}/orders/1

### Order 3 is Bob's -> 404 /problems/order/unknown
GET {{host}}/users/{{ada}}/orders/3

### Order 2 is open -> 204 the first time, 409 /problems/order/already-shipped after that
POST {{host}}/orders/2/ship

### Eve is an ordinary member -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/users/{{eve}}

### Ada is the last administrator -> 403 /problems/user/last-administrator, returned rather than thrown
DELETE {{host}}/users/{{ada}}

### The explanation for a type a caller received
GET {{host}}/problems/user/not-signed-up

### Every problem the application can produce
GET {{host}}/problems

### A deliberate failure to point client error handling at - development only
GET {{host}}/problems/expected/418

### The Swashbuckle document
GET {{host}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json

### The built-in document
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
